<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Noodle estimates raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Noodle estimates raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rodman &amp; Renshaw analyst Harry Ikenson said he raised estimates for Noodle Kidoodle Inc on Thursday after it posted first quarter earnings after the market close on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Company lost $0.16 a share compared with $0.22 a share excluding an item.  In a report, Ikenson said that was in line with his estimate and $0.02 above consensus. Net loss per share was $0.26 compared with $0.37.</p>
<p>-- raised Q2 loss estimate to $0.22 from $0.25; fiscal 1998 loss to $0.22 from $0.31; fiscal 1999 loss to $0.15 from $0.25.</p>
<p>-- Kept neutral rating.</p>
<p>-- Shares off 3/8 to 3-1/2.</p>
</text>
